For clarity:

(a) a student independently using the Software for that student’s own
    coursework or thesis may qualify for Permitted Individual Use;
(b) a school or university installing, deploying, administering, requiring,
    bundling, hosting, or operating the Software as an institutional resource
    is Organizational Use;
(c) a teacher, researcher, employee, contractor, or consultant using the
    Software as part of official duties is Organizational Use;
(d) a company using the Software for internal tools, client work, prototypes,
    products, services, SaaS, websites, or applications is Organizational
    Use; and
(e) a nonprofit, government body, association, foundation, laboratory, or
    other organized group is an Organization even if it does not operate for
    profit.

Organizational Use requires a Commercial License from the Licensor.

